  <static seed="626" source="Library/Michigan/Chap16Sec5/Q11.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate, in spherical coordinates, the triple integral of
<m>f(\rho,\theta,\phi) = \sin\phi</m>, over the region
<m>0 \le \theta \le 2\pi</m>,
<m>\pi/3 \le \phi \le \pi/2</m>,
<m>2 \le \rho \le 6</m>.</p>
<p>integral = <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\pi }{6}\mathopen{}\left(6^{3}-2^{3}\right)\mathopen{}\left(\pi +\sin\mathopen{}\left(\frac{2\pi }{3}\right)-\frac{2\pi }{3}\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\int_W f\,dV
   = \int_0^{2\pi} \int_{\pi/3}^{\pi/2} \int_{2}^{6}
	(\sin\phi)\rho^2 \sin \phi\,d\rho\,d\phi\,d\theta
   = \int_0^{2\pi} \int_{\pi/3}^{\pi/2}
	(\sin^2\phi)(\frac13)(\rho^3)\bigg|_{\rho=2}^{\rho=6}
	\,d\phi\,d\theta</me>
<me>= \frac{208}{3} \int_0^{2\pi} \int_{\pi/3}^{\pi/2} \frac12(1 - \cos2\phi)\, d\phi\,d\theta
   = \frac{208}{3} \int_0^{2\pi} \frac12(\phi - \frac12\sin2\phi)\bigg|_{\phi=\pi/3}^{\phi=\pi/2}\,d\theta</me>
<me>= \frac{52}{3} (\frac{\pi}3 + \frac{\sqrt3}2) \int_0^{2\pi}\frac12\,d\theta = \frac{52}{3} (\frac{\pi}3 + \frac{\sqrt3}2) \pi.</me>



</solution>
